{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_xgqh3dml4qntzryq275lqc3d2qleeeulknguumqr4y2zns6e7piq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_019kRt4VC79irH8BcqXAZzga","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\np='tests/phase_c_errors.rs'\ns=open(p).read()\nold = '''#[test]\nfn e25_zero_length_match_loops_forever() {\n    // lib.c:272 -- cp_len_base[29] == cp_len_base[30] == 0 with 0 extra bits, so\n    // length symbols 286 and 287 produce length 0: `s->out` never advances and\n    // no check fails. Both libraries must hang (SIGALRM from the worker).\n    for lsym in [29usize, 30] {'''\nnew = '''#[test]\nfn e25_zero_length_match_makes_no_progress() {\n    // lib.c:272 -- cp_len_base[29] == cp_len_base[30] == 0 with 0 extra bits, so\n    // length symbols 286 and 287 produce `length == 0`: `s->out` does not\n    // advance, `memset(dst, *src, 0)` copies nothing, and **no check fails** --\n    // the C accepts it. It is not a hang, because the symbol still consumes\n    // bits; both libraries must return 1 with identical output.\n    for lsym in [29usize, 30] {'''\nassert old in s\ns = s.replace(old, new)\nold2 = '''        w.bytes.extend_from_slice(&[0u8; 64]);\n        assert_signal_row(\n            Case::new(&format!(\"E25 length symbol {s} -> length 0\"), &w.bytes, 4096),\n            14,\n        );\n    }\n}'''\nnew2 = '''        w.bytes.extend_from_slice(&[0u8; 64]);\n        let case = Case::new(&format!(\"E25 length symbol {s} -> length 0\"), &w.bytes, 4096);\n        assert_error_row(case, 1, None);\n        // and at every alignment / output size\n        let mut cases = Vec::new();\n        for io in 0..4usize {\n            for out in [8i32, 9, 4096] {\n                cases.push(\n                    Case::new(&format!(\"E25 lensym={s} io={io} out={out}\"), &w.bytes, out)\n                        .in_off(io),\n                );\n            }\n        }\n        assert_batch_m