nclude/lib.h\nc_src/license.txt\nc_src/src/lib.c\n\n=== libloading in dev-dependencies ===\n[dev-dependencies]\nlibloading = \"0.8\"\n\n\n=== target artifacts ===\ntarget/c_build/libtranslated_rust.so\ntarget/cdylib_build/debug/libpinflate_lib.so\ntarget/debug/libpinflate_lib.so\ntarget/release/libpinflate_lib.so","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_wx2mt2lii7zjxscby2yo65cg2avdbhmf4ja4rrcwba6cvxmng42a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass, and `c_src/` is untouched.\n\n## What I found and fixed\n\nThe translation had **three real behavioural divergences**, all found by building the C exactly as the task prescribes and comparing through `dlopen`:\n\n**1. The reference C build has `assert()` enabled.** `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` sets no `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE`, so there's no `-DNDEBUG` and `nm -D` shows `U __assert_fail`. The ten `assert()`s in `lib.c` are caller-observable: hostile input prints a diagnostic and `abort()`s. The translation had reduced them to comments — on 250 fuzzed inputs, **89 (36%) diverged** (C → `SIGABRT`, Rust → clean return). Now reproduced via `cp_assert_fail()`, at the same line, in the same order. This included nailing `cp_decode`'s `assert((search >> len) == (key >> len))`, where `len` can be 32 and the C shift is undefined — `objdump` on the reference object shows gcc emits a variable `shr %cl`, so the count truncates mod 32.\n\n**2. `cp_dynamic`'s `lens[288+32]` overrun wedges the C library.** No run-length arm clamps `n`, so a run writes up to 137 bytes over `cp_dynamic`'s own locals — including `n` itself. The C **loops forever**; the Rust returned normally. `src/lib.rs` now models the frame exactly as gcc `-O0` emits it (offsets verified against `objdump -d`), so it wedges identically. As a bonus this made `lens[-1]` correct for free: it lands on the MSB of the spilled `s` pointer, always `0x00` on x86-64.\n\n**3. Rust's dev-profile UB checks** turned C's `SIGSEGV` on a `NULL in`/`out` into a Rust panic; `[profile.dev] debug-assertions = false` restores C-faithful behaviour.\n\n## The thing I'd flag most\n\n**Matching signals isn't enough.** My first suite passed while three injected bugs went undetected, because `SIGABRT == SIGABRT` hides two libraries aborting for *different reasons*. I now scrape the assert diagnostic (`lib.c:<line>: <func>: Assertion ...`) from the worker's stderr and compare that too. That closed all three gaps.\n\nI verified this with `verify/mutation_check.sh`, which injects 17 one-line bugs and requires the suite to fail for each: **17/17 detected, 0 blind spots**. It also taught me one mutation was *not* a bug — disabling the `memset` arm is unobservable, since for `backwards_distance == 1` the byte-copy loop propagates the same byte.\n\n## Results\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo test` | **64 passed, 0 failed** |\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | 8/8 symbols, **0 missing**, identical size/type/binding |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 40/40 rows ✅ |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 30/30 rows ✅ |\n| Feature combos | 1 (no `[features]`, no CMake options) — derived, not assumed |\n| Extra sweeps | 3 900 zlib streams + 2 500 fuzz cases + same again on `--release` → **0 divergences** |\n\nTwo notes on scope: there is exactly **one** build configuration, so the \"every feature combination\" gate is trivially satisfied — `d7_no_feature_flags_exist` will fail the build if a feature is ever added without extending the matrix. And a few deep-UB paths (`cp_build`'s `counts[]` overflow past index 56, `lens[]` overrun beyond the modelled frame) are documented in `ERRORS.md` as unmatchable-by-construction rather than papered over; the argument for why each is unreachable or harmless is written out there."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":899,"cache_read_input_tokens":412589,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":899,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6690c9e-476a-4013-b61c-2c21074bdc4a","uuid":"1cd33744-b264-49e0-8983-4420ec9cadf0","timestamp":"2026-08-20T15:22:01.652Z"}
